### List events

Events are listed by calendar, optionally bounded by a time range and a
free-text query.

### One event

### Create an event (write)

An event needs the calendar, a title, and RFC3339 start and end times,
optionally a description and attendees.

### Delete an event (destructive)

### Free/busy

Free/busy queries take an RFC3339 time range and one or more calendars.

## Output

Tool results are JSON. List tools return the items and whether more existed
past the limit; failures include Google's error (with `code` and `message`) —
surface the error rather than retrying blindly.

## Notes

- Times are RFC3339 (e.g. `2026-06-01T10:00:00Z`); event lists return expanded
  single instances ordered by start time.
